                "reply_count": 8,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "The Affordable Care Act simply isn\u2019t affordable, and health insurance premiums are spiking. Families in #CO03 shouldn\u2019t be hit by a system that\u2019s already failing them.\n\nI\u2019m part of a bipartisan group outlining a practical path forward on health care. Our bill, the Bipartisan HOPE Act, prevents those immediate hikes while adding real guardrails and accountability. It\u2019s a bridge that gives Congress the space to take on the real issue: underlying health care costs that keep rising year after year.\n\nThe ACA hasn\u2019t lived up to its name, but letting premiums jump overnight isn\u2019t an option. I\u2019m focused on helping families now and pushing for long-term reforms that actually lower costs. That\u2019s the work ahead.\n\nRead my full release on the Bipartisan HOPE Act here: https://t.co/JJwZExPAaR",
